* FD-03  Closed-loop common-mode input range (CMFB holding the output common mode)
* Spec 3.1.2, Fig. 27: a common-mode source drives both input resistors of the
* FD-01 network; DC sweep 0 .. VDD in 5 mV steps.  The output common mode
* should stay at VCOM: the slope of Vop (or Von) gives 1/CMRR and the range
* where that stays within 6 dB of its value at VCOM is the spec's range; the
* bench also reports the range where the output common mode moves by no more
* than 10 mV from its value at VCOM (robust when the CMFB makes the slope tiny).
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-7 abstol=1e-16 vntol=1e-10
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VI vi 0 {{VCM}}
R1 vi inp {{R_NET}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vi inn {{R_NET}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
dc vi 0 {{VDD}} 0.005
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn) v(inp) v(inn)
.endc
.end
